{
	"name": "AI video from a prompt to Reels, TikTok and Shorts, held for approval",
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "3deb4c26-e618-419e-aa3b-c6eb0db6fcf2",
			"name": "Overview",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-1000,
				-80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Turn a prompt into a short video, checked by you\n\n### How it works\n- Every 30 minutes it takes one row with Status **Ready**.\n- fal.ai makes a 9:16 video from the Prompt with Veo 3. It checks every minute, and stops after 15 tries.\n- sprkly pulls the finished video once, then schedules it to your Reels, TikTok and Shorts accounts 2 hours from now.\n- The post has **Requires Approval** on. sprkly emails you an Approve link. Watch the video, then approve it. Nothing goes out before that.\n- The AI lives in fal.ai. sprkly has no AI. It only publishes.\n- The row gets the video link, the sprkly Post ID and the job ID. When the post goes out, the row gets **Published** and the link.\n\n### Setup\n- Needs the n8n-nodes-sprkly community node (Settings, Community Nodes).\n- Logins: a sprkly API key, a Google login, a fal.ai key.\n- fal.ai bills you for every clip it makes. One row per run keeps the cost in check.\n- Make a Header Auth login: name `Authorization`, value: the word `Key`, a space, then your fal.ai key. Add it to the 3 fal.ai nodes.\n- Sheet columns: Status, Prompt, Caption, Title, Accounts, Job ID, Video URL, sprkly Post ID, Link, Error.\n- Accounts look like `instagram:myhandle, tiktok:myhandle, youtube:My channel`. Title is for TikTok and YouTube.\n- sprkly API docs: https://sprkly.app/docs/api\n- Node: https://github.com/ahlanlhw/n8n-nodes-sprkly\n\n### Customize\n- Change the model or the shape in **Start the video**.",
				"height": 900,
				"width": 520,
				"color": 1
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "b63974e5-e204-4a5e-8458-47937622a381",
			"name": "Note: make the video",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Make the video\nThe row is marked Making video first, so the next run skips it. The loop checks the job once a minute. After 15 checks it stops and writes an error, so a stuck job never runs forever.",
				"height": 640,
				"width": 1460,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "5624a36b-4b8b-4977-b6a1-97fe8043b53d",
			"name": "Note: publish",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				1060,
				80
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Hold it for approval\nsprkly pulls the file once from fal.ai and makes one post for every account. External ID aivideo plus the job ID means a re-run never posts twice.",
				"height": 640,
				"width": 1220,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "b38fc0be-78f5-4950-bdaf-e992ad9bbbad",
			"name": "Note: track posts",
			"type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
			"typeVersion": 1,
			"position": [
				-440,
				800
			],
			"parameters": {
				"content": "## Track what went out\nWhen the video goes out or fails, the row is found by its Job ID and gets the status and the link.",
				"height": 440,
				"width": 1000,
				"color": 7
			}
		},
